     (`List (Nat × RtVal)`), disjoint `EffectLog` heap slots (`log1 = .heapPtr 0`, `log2 = .heapPtr 1`),
     and global chronological event observer (`obsEvents : List Nat`).
     Never dispatches on package-level header flags (`preserveUb`, `monoComplete`) or
     hardcoded outcomes.
  2. Proves the frozen C0 independent endpoint (`docs/rust-opsem/c0-scope-and-frozen-endpoint.md`)
     with disjoint `log1` and `log2` storage (`R2`), finite-width `u32`/`usize` arithmetic including
     `align_to(usize::MAX - 1, 4) = Err(SizeError)` and `Arguments::from_str` vs `panic_fmt`
     separation (`R3`), and an unconditional all-prefix theorem (`∀ n : Nat`) for the unmodified
     captured loop `unbounded_period4_probe` (`R4`).
  3. Executes the matched-scope Charon `0.1.210` `.amir` v3 packages through the exact same
     byte parser and operational interpreter on the identical disjoint-storage and chronological
     C0 endpoint:
     - Raw Charon ULLBC (`charonUllbcCleanupRawBytes`): decodes as well-formed `.amir` v3 and
       fails at runtime with `.missingBody` because `core::mem::drop` is opaque and
       compiler-synthesized drop-glue bodies (`Guard`, `PairGuards`) are omitted.
     - Charon ULLBC + Remedy R2 (`charonUllbcCleanupRemedyR2Bytes`): decodes via `parseWirePackage`
       and satisfies all 6 normal and unwind C0 cleanup specifications (both disjoint `log1`/`log2`
       residual states and global chronological `obsEvents`) identically to Direct MIR.
     - Charon Structured LLBC + Remedy R2 (`charonLlbcCleanupRemedyR2Bytes`): decodes via
       `parseWirePackage`, satisfies all 3 normal-return C0 cleanup cases, and fails all 3
       unwind-cleanup C0 cases because `ullbc_to_llbc` strips `on_unwind` cleanup edges.
     - Charon ULLBC + Remedy R1 (`charonUllbcPlaceMentionR1Bytes`): decodes via `parseWirePackage`
       and satisfies all 6 `place_mention_probe` UB-detection cases identically to Direct MIR.
-/

